# BRANDSWOT Modular — pixel source (source of truth for the whole family)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Designed by Gowtham Sai · BRANDSWOT Consultancy · Hyderabad, India
# Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (see ../OFL.txt)
#
# HOW IT WORKS
#   Every letter is drawn on a pixel grid.  One pixel = 100 × 99 font units,
#   filled with three courses of running-bond brickwork (bricks 40 × 23,
#   mortar 10).  build_ufos.py lays the bricks, adds every accented letter,
#   and writes the Light / Bold / Black masters for the variable font.
#
# FORMAT
#   glyph <name> [U+XXXX] y=<n>     y = pixel row of the bottom line (0 = baseline)
#   rows follow top → bottom, '#' = pixel on, '.' = off
#   mark  <name> cc=<col> pos=top|bottom|ogonek
#
# To edit a letter: change the #'s, run `make build`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

